Stage 0 verified local numeric baseline, 2026-11-03.
Households: CRRA EGM, Rouwenhorst idiosyncratic shocks, capital savings; stationary rational expectations.
Firms: Cobb–Douglas, competitive wage and interest rate. Market clearing: K supply=demand and Y=C+delta K.
Numerical tests: all 6 unittest passed. Capital relative residual 2.31e-8, goods residual 5.35e-9, weighted p99 KKT/Euler residual 7.94e-7; zero upper-edge mass.
Sensitivity: na in 200/360/520, nz in 5/7, asset maximum in 600/900; reports committed.
Limitations: no aggregate risk, no proof of mathematical equilibrium uniqueness, no finite population price re-clearing.
Stage 2 priority: voluntary bilateral matching and trading with distinct liquidity preferences/assets and explicit participation constraints; do not treat arbitrary zero-sum swaps as utility-maximizing trades.
